//RS /// The one Ctrl-C consumption rule: take the whole pending count, then run
//RS /// every registered handler once per counted interrupt, in registration order.
//RS ///
//RS /// An empty `handlers` slice does NOT consume. The count is process-wide and
//RS /// shared, so a drain with nothing registered must leave the signal for the
//RS /// drain that can actually deliver it.
